{"name":"Dreamweaver","hex":"#ccc6d7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Dreamweaver (Sabbat album)","blocks":[{"text":"Dreamweaver (Reflections of Our Yesterdays) is the second full-length album by the British thrash metal band Sabbat, released in 1989"}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/ce/Sabbatdreamweaverreflectionofouryesterdayrr5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dreamweaver_(Sabbat_album)"},{"title":"Dreamweaver (George Duke album)","blocks":[{"text":"DreamWeaver is a final studio album by American keyboardist and record producer George Duke. It was released on July 16, 2013, through Big Piano Music and Heads Up International. Recording sessions for the album took place at Le Gonks West in Los Angeles, California. The album is dedicated to Corine Duke, who died in 2011."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d7/George_Duke_-_Dreamweaver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dreamweaver_(George_Duke_album)"},{"title":"Adobe Dreamweaver","blocks":[{"text":"Adobe Dreamweaver is a proprietary web development tool from Adobe. It was created by Macromedia in 1997 and developed by them until Macromedia was acquired by Adobe Systems in 2005."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Adobe_Dreamweaver_CC_icon.svg/330px-Adobe_Dreamweaver_CC_icon.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adobe_Dreamweaver"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b6/Default_Dreamweaver_2020_screen.png/330px-Default_Dreamweaver_2020_screen.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b6/Default_Dreamweaver_2020_screen.png/330px-Default_Dr